b04f53ae439123bb9bca7129b896378bbad300a7 blob 6863
# F222 / F223 / F224: material candidates not established

These are **three bounded source/materiality rejections**, not measured no-gain results or claims that the code has no cost. No candidate, product test or comparison ran.

| Finding | Actual producer and bounded conclusion |
| --- | --- |
| F222 | The generic XML comparer serializes on `GetHashCode`, but the actual `Store_Then_Get` Fact compares two/three simple elements through arrays and real repository-produced read-only lists. The declared xUnit source's linear-container path uses element equality; its custom-comparer set path can hash. No actual large hashing producer or material candidate was established, and universal hash-call absence is not claimed. |
| F223 | Non-error diagnostic filtering repeatedly queries supported descriptors. Both component analyzer getters call `ImmutableArray.Create` with one descriptor per access; the route-handler analyzer instead retains eight descriptors. The original scan's blanket retained-array explanation was too broad. Actual getter/scan cost remains unmeasured within real compiler/test work. |
| F224 | Each retained source diagnostic enumerates every supplied project's documents, requests each syntax tree and adds for every match. Actual one-/two-document test producers were traced. Repeated requests are real, but source does not prove reparsing or material whole-test cost. This is distinct from F223 despite the shared file/card. |

## Exact evidence and scope

Original: `37e809ead5824bc753a1c3d56f11615bdb1296c5`. Fresh upstream `main`: `d3483989953ae3cccd773aea5ea04cb0c7198531`. The reserved F145 checkout supplied navigation/object storage, not Default.

[Raw membership proof](source-membership.json) retains **46 whole ASP.NET captures through 63 raw commit/tree/blob objects**, exact file modes and exact captured bytes: 23 paths for each role. The portable verifier separately reads every captured artifact and matches its blob/hash/length to that graph. Whole source copies include actual XML repository/tests, real analyzer producers/descriptors/runners, project creation, embedded source examples and project/version metadata.

[Collection273](evidence/source273/COLLECTION.json) ran once and returned zero: 22 waited Git/gh source roots, five initial common source fingerprints and five navigation-only guidance snapshots. Its historical `assessment pending` field remains unchanged. [Entry qualification274](evidence/source274/ASSERTION-ENTRY.json) ran once and returned zero: two additional whole external files and one release-tree request. The declared xUnit 2.9.2 release points its assertion submodule at `cac8b688c193c0f244a0bedf3bb60feeb32d377a`. Seven [external whole-file fingerprints](external-source.json) and pinned API responses are witnesses, **not a full raw external commit/tree graph or selected executing binary**.

[Final assessment](evidence/parent275/ASSESSMENT.json), [archive observation](evidence/parent275/ARCHIVE.json), [complete copied evidence index](evidence-index.json) and [actual enclosing completion](preparation-terminal.json) distinguish source qualification from product execution. Six final packaging Git metadata roots bring the source/packaging total to 31; no product-native roots or comparison authorizations were consumed.

The separate [upstream license notice](licenses/xunit-assert/LICENSE.txt) is copied verbatim from the same pinned assertion revision. Its [additive qualification](licenses/xunit-assert/LICENSE-SOURCE.json) uses one further read-only request, bringing the collection/packaging/licensing total to 32 roots. It does not change the earlier 240-file evidence index, source inputs or executed helpers.

## Producer and semantic boundaries

F222's real repository clones elements on storage and returns a read-only list of fresh deep copies. The only two direct comparer references found by the recorded exact Default search are the two collection assertions in `Store_Then_Get`; this lexical result is not a universal consumer-absence proof. The helper also uses filtered/sorted sequence equality for XML nodes/attributes. Preserve semantic equality, comment/xmlns treatment, attribute order handling, duplicate/order behavior, diagnostics and hashing contracts; do not invent large XML/hash-set workloads or mix in an unrelated equality/hash change.

For F223, actual `InternalUsageAnalyzer` operation/symbol callbacks report enabled BL0006 warnings. Component declaration/body tests each pass one source and assert six/five output diagnostics. These are source expectations, not measured incoming compiler diagnostic counts or executed output counts. Error diagnostics bypass the supported-descriptor getter. The helper is a nonshipping `netstandard2.0` test asset with public/protected entry points, not proof of no external consumers or a universal descriptor bound.

For F224, two real route-handler Facts each provide two sources and assert one diagnostic. Their runner calls `DiagnosticProject.Create`, then adds metadata references, not extra source documents. `DiagnosticProject` caches reference-only base solutions by assembly and adds one document per input source. Preserve match multiplicity, project/document enumeration, final stable `SourceSpan.Start` ordering, None/metadata shortcuts, deferred/getter failure timing and the existing all/analyzer-diagnostic branch. Do not assume one match universally or silently fix the separate string-overload `getAllDiagnostics` forwarding omission.

## Unrun product tests

The explicit source-only scope prohibited product execution; no selected unchanged Original/Default product-test graph was authorized here. These existing tests were **read, not run**:

- `EphemeralXmlRepositoryTests.Store_Then_Get`.
- `ComponentInternalUsageDiagnosticsAnalyzerTest.InternalUsage_FindsUseOfInternalTypesInDeclarations`.
- `ComponentInternalUsageDiagnosticsAnalyzerTest.InternalUsage_FindsUseOfInternalTypesInMethodBody`.
- `DisallowReturningActionResultsFromMapMethodsTest.MinimalAction_ReturningActionResultOfTFromANonLocalFunction_ProducesDiagnostics`.
- `DisallowReturningActionResultsFromMapMethodsTest.MinimalAction_ReturningActionResultOfTDeclarationInDifferentFile_ProducesDiagnostics`.

The observed faithful boundary is whole real producer/caller/test source, not a passing runtime assertion, red/green fix, allocation result or timing result. No artificial diagnostic/document/XML cardinalities or repeated compilation loops justified a performance proposal.

Run the portable read-only audit:

```text
node verify.mjs
```

Final issue/index linkage is additive. Rejections create no performance PR/window; the fixed historical REPORT and its browser window stay untouched. Root/stream receipts do not assert a universal descendant census, machine idleness, dedicated host or uninterrupted 24/7 execution.

